 "notes": [
  "A turn is the history rendered with the turn's message minus the generation prompt, minus the end-of-sentence token, which the stop decoder hides from the parser.",
  "The encoder ends the prompt with <think> in thinking mode and </think> in chat mode, after the last user message and again after a tool result (inside the same assistant turn, after </function_results>).",
  "The two newlines the encoder writes before a calls block are the content's where the content stay already holds text (the turn's own content, or the prompt's text after a tool result in chat mode, which the replay walks); alone at a stay's start they are the encoder's spacing, dropped. The encoder's parser looks for the block after them either way. `content` is the table's reading and `reference_content` the parser's.",
  "The tail is the prompt from its last user message; the replay walks it from the last <｜Assistant｜>."
 ],
